course: dictionary
lesson: 15880
title: Informed and uninformed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uninformed means not knowing the facts about something. When you have not found out the facts, you are uninformed. «Sam gave an uninformed guess about the winner.» Sam did not know the facts, so the guess was made without knowledge.
explain: An informed opinion is based on facts. An uninformed opinion is made without enough knowledge. «The judge made an informed decision after reading every letter.» She read the facts first, so her decision was informed.
explain: You often meet uninformed with the word about, as in «uninformed about the rules». Read the sentence around it. The clues tell you whether someone knows the facts or not.
explain: A quick check is to swap in the phrase «without enough knowledge». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Uninformed means not knowing the facts about something.
fact: «An uninformed guess» is a guess made without knowing the facts.
fact: An informed opinion is based on facts; an uninformed opinion is made without enough knowledge.
fact: «Don't make uninformed decisions» means find out the facts first.
fact: Phrases to remember: «uninformed about», «an uninformed guess», «uninformed opinion».
exercise: «Ben made an uninformed guess about the weather.» What does uninformed mean here? | Made after reading the weather report | Made with a big smile | Made very loudly | *Made without knowing the facts
exercise: Which of these is an informed opinion? | A joke you tell at lunch | A feeling you cannot explain | *An opinion based on facts | An opinion made with no facts at all
exercise: Which word means not knowing the facts about something? | opinion | informed | facts | *uninformed
test: «Lily was uninformed about the bus times, so she missed the first one.» What does uninformed about mean here? | *Did not know the facts about the bus times | Was angry about the bus | Knew the bus times very well | Liked the bus driver
test: Mum says, «Don't make uninformed decisions.» What should you do instead? | *Find out the facts first | Decide quickly and never change your mind | Ask your friend to decide for you | Choose the one with the nicest picture
exam: «The coach gave an uninformed opinion about the match, because he had not watched a single game.» Why was the opinion uninformed? | It was about the weather | *He did not know the facts, because he had not watched the games | It was based on facts from the newspaper | It was a very long opinion
